3GPP RRC ASN.1
--------------

rust/crates/umts-rrc-schema/schema/rrc.asn1 contains the ASN.1 modules of
3GPP TS 25.331 v19.0.1, clause 11. The specification is copyright of the 3GPP
Organizational Partners. The file is included to generate the RRC
message types and is not covered by this project's license.

Rust RRC codecs
---------------

RRC bindings are generated at build time with rasn-compiler and use the rasn
runtime, both licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

rasn-compiler is fetched from the umts branch of
https://github.com/chrismoos/rasn-compiler, a fork of
https://github.com/librasn/compiler containing two default-generation fixes.
Its source retains the original attribution and license texts.
Cargo.lock records the resolved commit.

Third-party libraries
---------------------

Rust dependencies are listed with their versions in Cargo.lock and keep
their own licenses. The DSP crates use wide, safe_arch and bytemuck for SIMD
arithmetic, each licensed under Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

Native libraries are provisioned separately and linked only when the matching
build option is selected:

  - UHD / libuhd (USRP backend)
        License: GPL-3.0-or-later
        By Ettus Research / National Instruments.
  - libbladeRF (bladeRF backend)
        License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
        By Nuand LLC.
  - SoapySDR (optional backend)
        License: Boost Software License 1.0
  - usrsctp (userspace SCTP transport)
        License: BSD-3-Clause

License compatibility:
  - GPL-3.0-or-later (UHD) combines with AGPL-3.0-or-later under AGPLv3
    section 13. A build that links UHD distributes under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  - LGPL-2.1-or-later (libbladeRF) permits use by a program under any license.
    The LGPL terms continue to apply to libbladeRF itself.
  - The Boost and BSD licenses are permissive.

The combined umts-hnb binary distributes under AGPL-3.0-or-later. AGPL
section 13 (network-use source offer) applies to anyone hosting umts-hnb as a
service.

